# The extensionless wmux CLI shim is a bash script — force LF so its shebang
# runs under bash even on Windows with core.autocrlf=true.
src/cli-bin/wmux text eol=lf

# ...and its cmd.exe twin needs the opposite, explicitly. cmd.exe parses a .cmd
# by byte offset assuming CRLF: fed LF-only it resumes mid-token, so `setlocal`
# runs as `tlocal` and `REM` as `M`. It half-works — the last line still
# executes — which is exactly why nobody notices. This has been riding on
# core.autocrlf=true; a clone with autocrlf=false shipped a broken shim.
src/cli-bin/wmux.cmd text eol=crlf
resources/shell-integration/wmux-cmd-integration.cmd text eol=crlf
src/shell-integration/wmux-cmd-integration.cmd text eol=crlf
